WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.770
Every token in this
book assumes the device

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.188
on the wire is the device it claims to be.

3
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:10.100
802.1X turns that assumption
into a proof at the switch port.

4
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:15.900
Use EAP-TLS, mutual certificate
authentication, for every managed device.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.190
Password methods are failing on their own:

6
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.421
Credential Guard blocks
PEAP-MSCHAPv2 single sign-on,

7
00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:29.625
and the October 2026 Windows update
restricts NTLMv1-derived credentials too.

8
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:32.257
The RADIUS server is
usually the last piece

9
00:00:32.257 --> 00:00:34.963
of the network standing
on Active Directory.

10
00:00:34.963 --> 00:00:38.647
Windows NPS authorizes
against AD computer objects,

11
00:00:38.647 --> 00:00:41.662
and Entra joined devices
don't support that.

12
00:00:41.662 --> 00:00:46.574
There's no Entra RADIUS product;
the NPS extension adds MFA,

13
00:00:46.574 --> 00:00:49.950
but NPS still authenticates against AD.

14
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.205
And NPS has no posture engine:

15
00:00:52.205 --> 00:00:57.937
Network Access Protection was deprecated
back in Windows Server 2012 R2.

16
00:00:57.937 --> 00:01:04.009
So posture comes from Intune's compliance
retrieval service, read by a NAC platform,

17
00:01:04.009 --> 00:01:09.376
and each device lands in production,
remediation, quarantine, guest or IoT.

18
00:01:09.376 --> 00:01:13.940
After the Blast-RADIUS attack, require
Message-Authenticator everywhere.
